# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./install.sh at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
name: xymonapi
version: 2.3.0
side: server, client
summary: a read-only HTTP and JSON interface to a Xymon server, as one of its xymonlaunch tasks, and its client
requires: on the server, xymon >= 4.3.31 (main); python >= 3.9
manual: xymonapi.8

# How ./install.sh installs it. A plugin ships profiles, one per kind of
# place, each a set of PROFILE-* keys; the script learns the profile names
# from the files, so a plugin may declare one of its own, in letters,
# digits and underscores: the dash is what joins a plugin's name to a
# profile's in xymonapi-mcp-tools. PROFILE-root is
# where it goes: ext, $XYMONHOME/ext/NAME on a Xymon machine; prefix,
# $PREFIX/libexec/xymon-plugins/NAME on your own machine, as yourself.
# PROFILE-roles names the roles of a machine that bring the profile when
# none is said: server, client, tools. Then the files copied beside the
# plugin's others, the manual page, the modules its Python needs (offered
# at install time), the command put in $PREFIX/bin and the script it runs,
# the xymonlaunch task, the web server snippets kept once written, the
# program whose running process an install stops, a note for the venv
# offer, and the messages after an install and a removal, which may name
# @ETC@, @TASKDIR@ and @XYMONHOME@. executable lists the files made 755,
# the others 644; needs, the plugins installed first, beside it.
server-root: ext
server-roles: server
server-files: app.py xymon.py xymonapi_client.py tokens.py openapi.yaml requirements.txt xymonapi.sh
server-manual: xymonapi.8
server-modules: fastapi uvicorn yaml
server-task: xymonapi.tasks.DIST
server-conf: xymonapi-apache.conf xymonapi-nginx.conf xymonapi-lighttpd.conf
server-restart: app.py
server-installed: Installed. Enable the API: remove DISABLED from @TASKDIR@/xymonapi. For other machines, include one of
server-installed:   @ETC@/xymonapi-{apache,nginx,lighttpd}.conf in the web server, or give the API xymond's certificate: see xymonapi(8).
server-removed: Removed xymonapi. Kept, for you to remove: @ETC@/xymonapi-{apache,nginx,lighttpd}.conf --
server-removed:   take its Include out of the web server first -- and the tokens file, $XYMONAPI_TOKENS
server-removed:   ($XYMONVAR/xymonapi/tokens by default).
tools-root: prefix
tools-roles: tools
tools-files: xymonapi_client.py xymonapi-connect.sh
tools-manual: xymonapi-connect.1
tools-command: xymonapi-connect xymonapi-connect.sh
executable: xymonapi.sh xymonapi-connect.sh
tools-removed: Removed xymonapi's client. Kept: the tokens in ~/.config/xymon-api/, which the API's /tokens revokes.
